# day_trader_pro/.gitignore — 2026-07-29 — + the two harvested-artifact roots
# (signal_journal/, chain_snapshots/) and delivered archives.
# 2026-07-14 — layout consolidation:
# every data-collection root stays LOCAL ONLY; the repo carries code, not tape.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# ── data products (consolidated 2026-07-14) — never committed ─────────────────
ohlc/
trades/
reports/

# harvested per-box artifacts (harvest v0.5.0 / v0.5.1 / v0.6.0) — LOCAL ONLY.
# Excluded BY FOLDER, deliberately, rather than by extension: a blanket *.json
# or *.db rule would also silently swallow a legitimate file added later, and a
# rule that hides things without saying so is the exact failure mode that cost
# three sessions of chains. Anything genuinely meant for the repo stays visible.
#   signal_journal/<date>/<SYM>.jsonl      — scored/disposition/readiness rows
#   chain_snapshots/<date>/<SYM>.jsonl.gz  — ~1.4MB/box/day, unreconstructable
signal_journal/
chain_snapshots/

# legacy locations (pre-consolidation stragglers; migrate_data_layout.sh empties them)
pulls/
data/harvest/

# operational state (local runtime files)
data/instance_map.json
data/mock_state.json
data/report.json
data/selection_log.jsonl
# dtp r361 / CND.6 — who the purge budget skipped, rewritten every close. The
# `*` covers the atomic-write .tmp. Tracked, it would be dirty after every close
# and exactly what a discard recipe restores away (dtp r360).
data/purge_debt.json*
# r401 / OPS.26 — the boot raiser's status stamp. Runtime state, per-box,
# never shipped. Listed by NAME because this file ignores data/ per file
# rather than wholesale, and [[LVL.19]] is what forgetting the line costs:
# r379 shipped a reader and left its directory untracked AND unignored.
data/AGENT_STATUS
*.patch
*.csv

# delivered archives land in ~ but are sometimes unpacked in place
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# control-local, never fleet-synced
trades.db
MANIFEST.txt

# dtp r238 — warehouse_cache scratch. Disk-backed and self-deleting, but a
# crashed process between mkdtemp and its handler could leave one behind, and
# a multi-GB cache must never be committable.
var/

# 🔴 r360 — RUNTIME LOGS ARE NOT SOURCE. `logs/eod_conductor.log` was TRACKED
# and every close appends to it, so any failed land counted it as extract
# debris and the discard recipe restored it to its committed version — two
# nights of conductor output lost, and the file later read as if it were the
# record. A tracked log is not a record: it is a file with a history something
# else can rewrite. (Untracked by hand at dtp r360; this keeps it out.)
logs/
